The legal text is the Constitution of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, as published by the General Court of Massachusetts at
https://malegislature.gov/Laws/Constitution , read from the Common Crawl capture of 15 October 2026 (crawl CC-MAIN-2026-43).

The site's reuse terms could not be read from the network this build ran on. The Constitution is an official legal text of the
Commonwealth; the text of laws and constitutions is not copyrightable in the United States (Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, Inc.,
590 U.S. 255 (2020)). The robots.txt captured with the page allows all access. The text is republished here with credit to the
General Court of Massachusetts as its publisher.

The General Laws chapters are the text published by the General Court at https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws ,
read from Common Crawl and Internet Archive captures of its section pages (2025 and 2026). Statute text is not
copyrightable in the United States (Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, above); no annotations are used.

